# This repository's working tree is CRLF, matching GnollHack, MobileGnollHackLogger,
# and the shared plans repository. Content is stored LF-normalized in Git; only the
# checkout is CRLF. The explicit eol is required, not decorative: core.autocrlf is
# false on these machines, so without it Git performs no conversion at all and the
# checkout simply inherits the stored LF.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Redundant under the blanket rule above, kept explicit so that changing the blanket
# rule can never silently alter what PowerShell tooling receives.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# EXEMPTIONS -- consumed by GitHub Actions on ubuntu-latest, where CRLF breaks.
# A workflow checked out with CRLF feeds a trailing "\r" into every `run:` block and
# bash fails with: $'\r': command not found.
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Executed by the CI job on Linux. Python tolerates CRLF, but keeping it LF avoids
# depending on that tolerance and survives the file ever being run via a shebang.
*.py text eol=lf
